  "title": "Your first class",
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "shared",
      "heading": "Before you start",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "text": "Read the module README first. This section is the author's, not the archive's, and the builder uses this array verbatim (SF-10b)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "lang",
      "lang": "java",
      "heading": "Your first class",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Your first class"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "text": "A class is a name plus the state and behaviour filed under it. Start with the smallest one that compiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "text": "public final class Greeter {\n    public String greet(String who) {\n        return \"Hello, \" + who;\n    }\n}\n"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "Declare the class.",
            "Give it one method.",
            "Write the test before the body."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "text": "A method you cannot name is a method you do not yet understand."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Name it.",
                "Then write it."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "practice",
      "lang": "java",
      "key": "practice-java",
      "heading": "Practice: Greeter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Problem statement"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "text": "Make `Greeter.greet` return `Hello, <who>` for any non-empty name."
        },
        {
          "type": "disclosure",
          "summary": "Show a hint",
          "open": false,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "text": "Concatenation is enough. The grader shipped with the material checks the exact string."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Lesson: Your first class"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "text": "The test class shipped with the material is the grader. It is authoritative because nobody here wrote it (R5)."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Starting code"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "text": "public final class Greeter {\n    public String greet(String who) {\n        // your code here\n    }\n}\n"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
